    "updated_at": "2016-06-14T07:02:22Z",
    "body": "The other common case where this is a problem for people is that they use `--` in their IDs or class names, and want to be able to put their IDs or class names inside HTML comments. There is a CSS naming scheme called \"BEM\" that recommends putting `--` in class names. I think it is more useful to be able to do that than have to somehow \"escape\" the double-dash, or stop using the checker since it's complaining about non-problems.\n\nYou can think it's a trivial thing, but many trivial things that are useless errors in a checker makes the checker itself useless, in my opinion.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
